Description: library for your recent and favorite files
 Sheaf shows the files you opened recently and the ones you marked as
 favorites, whether they are documents, PDFs, books, pictures, audio or video,
 with thumbnails, tags, groups and fast search. It reads the standard recent
 files list that other applications already write, so there is nothing to
 set up.
 .
 It works on any desktop that follows the freedesktop standards, including
 GNOME, KDE Plasma, Xfce and Cinnamon. There is also a command line tool and a
 quick open popup, and it can import favorites and groups from Linux Mint
 Thingy.
